# Kubernetes adapter (cluster decouple)

This rule scopes AGENTS.md hard rule **28** (added in M4): every
cluster-side operation in AQP — Kafka admin, Flink session jobs,
deployment scaling, pod logs, manifest apply — flows through the
[`KubernetesAdapter`](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/protocol.py) abstraction.

The abstraction lets AQP run fully standalone (no cluster), attach to
the rpi_kubernetes management API, run inside a cluster with the
official Kubernetes Python SDK, or treat the local Docker Compose
stack as the cluster surface. The narrative walk-through lives in
[aqp_docs/docs/concepts/infrastructure/kubernetes-adapter.md](mdc:aqp_docs/docs/concepts/infrastructure/kubernetes-adapter.md).

## Hard rules

1. **One adapter surface.** Every cluster-side operation in AQP goes
   through
   [`get_kubernetes_adapter()`](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/protocol.py). Don't
   import
   [`ClusterMgmtClient`](mdc:aqp/services/cluster_mgmt_client.py)
   directly outside
   [`aqp/kubernetes/adapters/rpi_cluster.py`](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/adapters/rpi_cluster.py).
   That adapter is the only allowed wrapper.
2. **Adapters register themselves.** Concrete
   [`KubernetesAdapter`](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/protocol.py) subclasses set
   `adapter_kind` (`none` / `rpi_cluster` / `in_cluster` /
   `local_compose`) and the :class:`KubernetesAdapterMeta` metaclass
   auto-registers via
   `aqp.core.registry.register(kind="k8s_adapter")`. Don't decorate
   manually.
3. **`is_available()` is the gate.** Routes call `is_available()`
   first and translate `False` to `HTTP 503`. Failures during a
   live call surface as `KubernetesAdapterError` and translate to
   `HTTP 502`. Never let a raw cluster-mgmt HTTPError leak to the
   route layer.
4. **Auto-promote rpi when configured.** If
   `settings.kubernetes_adapter` is empty and
   `settings.cluster_mgmt_url` is set, the
   [`RpiClusterAdapter`](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/adapters/rpi_cluster.py)
   activates. This preserves the existing behaviour of "set the URL
   and the proxy works".
5. **Adapter calls re-read settings.** The
   [`RpiClusterAdapter`](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/adapters/rpi_cluster.py)
   builds a fresh underlying client per call so dynamic config /
   test isolation works without explicit cache invalidation. Don't
   cache an adapter's underlying transport across settings changes.
6. **Unsupported ops raise
   :class:`KubernetesAdapterUnavailable`.** When an adapter cannot
   service a method (e.g. local-compose has no Strimzi to talk to),
   raise the unavailable subclass — routes catch it and return 503.
   Don't return empty stubs; failure should be loud and
   gracefully-degraded.
7. **The native Kafka / Flink admin still wins.** The fallback
   pattern is `native -> adapter`. Native admin lives in
   [`aqp/streaming/admin/`](mdc:aqp/streaming/admin); the adapter
   is the cluster proxy when native isn't reachable. Don't swap that
   order.

## Adapter capabilities matrix

| Capability | None | RpiCluster | InCluster | LocalCompose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `is_available()` | False | URL set | kubeconfig loaded | docker on PATH |
| `kafka_*` | 503 | yes (HTTP) | 503 | 503 |
| `flink_*` | 503 | yes (HTTP) | 503 | 503 |
| `alphavantage_*` | 503 | yes (HTTP) | 503 | 503 |
| `scale_deployment` | 503 | yes | yes (AppsV1) | yes (compose up --scale) |
| `pod_logs` | 503 | (via supervisor) | yes | yes (compose logs) |
| `apply_manifest` | 503 | (out of scope) | yes | (out of scope) |

Filling in more "503" cells is fine — open a PR adding the method to
the relevant adapter and to the ABC.

## Where things live

| Need | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Adapter ABC + metaclass | [aqp/kubernetes/protocol.py](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/protocol.py) |
| None / Rpi / InCluster / LocalCompose | [aqp/kubernetes/adapters/](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/adapters) |
| `/cluster/*` REST surface | [aqp/api/routes/cluster_mgmt.py](mdc:aqp/api/routes/cluster_mgmt.py) |
| Native Kafka / Flink fallback | [aqp/api/routes/kafka.py](mdc:aqp/api/routes/kafka.py), [aqp/api/routes/flink.py](mdc:aqp/api/routes/flink.py) |
| Producer supervisor (kubernetes runtime) | [aqp/streaming/producers/supervisor.py](mdc:aqp/streaming/producers/supervisor.py) |
| FinOps audit (in-cluster path) | [aqp/tasks/finops_tasks.py](mdc:aqp/tasks/finops_tasks.py) — currently uses the kubernetes SDK directly because it needs list APIs not on the adapter; expanding the adapter is the migration target |

## Don't

- Don't import
  [`ClusterMgmtClient`](mdc:aqp/services/cluster_mgmt_client.py)
  outside the rpi adapter. Audit hook:
  `rg "from aqp.services.cluster_mgmt_client" --type py`.
- Don't call `kubernetes.client.*Api()` directly outside
  [`aqp/kubernetes/adapters/in_cluster.py`](mdc:aqp/kubernetes/adapters/in_cluster.py)
  (the existing call site in
  [`aqp/tasks/finops_tasks.py`](mdc:aqp/tasks/finops_tasks.py) is
  grandfathered until the adapter exposes list APIs).
- Don't reach for `subprocess.run("docker compose ...")` outside the
  local-compose adapter.
- Don't cache an adapter on a service object — always go through
  `get_kubernetes_adapter()` so settings changes propagate.

Consider these rules if they affect your changes.
